nd intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le09ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Language for Agreeing and Disagreeing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In English, when people give an opinion, it is important to show that you either agree or don't agree with it. There are many different ways in which we can show agreement and disagreement in English. Here are some of them:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Agreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Disagreeing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">(That's a) good point. <br/> (That's) so true. <br/> I feel the same way. <br/> I'm sure you are right. <br/> That's my opinion too. <br/> I see what you mean. <br/> I can see your point now. <br/> I don't disagree with that. <br/> </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Not necessarily. <br/>(But) don't you think that ...? <br/> (But) what about ... ? <br/> I don't really agree. <br/> I'm not sure that's always the case. <br/> The way I see it \u2026 <br/> I'd like to agree (with you), but \u2026<br/> That's really not how I see it, I'm afraid. <br/> You could say that, but \u2026\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Note:</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, the word \u201cagree\u201d is not used with the verb \u201cto be\u201d. Notice how the word \u201cagree\u201d is used:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><strike>I'm agree with you.</strike></li><li>I agree with you.</li><li><strike>I'm not agree with what you're saying.</strike></li><li>I do not agree with what you're saying.</li></ul>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for and Giving Opinions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In the business world, it is common to give your opinion about things. However, it is advisable to ask another person about their thoughts on something before you tell them how you feel about something. Here are some ways in which you can ask and give opinions."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking for Opinions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Opinions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>What's your idea for \u2026 ?</li> <li>What do you think of \u2026 ?</li> <li>What do you think about \u2026 ?</li> <li>How do you reckon \u2026 ?</li> <li>How d'you feel (about ... )?</li> <li>What's your idea of \u2026 ?</li> <li>What's your opinion of \u2026 ?</li> <li>(What do think about) that?</li> <li>Could you elaborate on that?</li> <li>Where do you stand (on \u2026 )?</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I reckon \u2026  As far as I know, \u2026<br/> If you ask me, \u2026 <br/> Personally, <br/> To my mind, <br/> The way I see it, \u2026 <br/>  To be honest / frank \u2026 <br/> In my view, \u2026 <br/>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">NOTE:</span><br/>When giving or asking for someone's opinion, it is also important to know how the word \u201copinion\u201d is used and what prepositions go with the word. Here are some examples: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">opinion of:</span><br/><span class =\"italic\">What's your <span class=\"strong\">opinion of</span> Farmani's latest clothing line?</span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">opinion on:</span><br/><span class =\"italic\">Farmani's <span class=\"strong\">opinions on</span> our services are important.</span></li>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Where do you stand on our new clothing line?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In my view, this strategy works best with what we are trying to do."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "core value"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a belief that an organization views as very important "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One of our company's core values is \u201cTest everything: assume nothing.\u201d "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you can use in a meeting."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "angle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a specific way of approaching a problem"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You never know what angle is going to work best until you test it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to translate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to convert into another form"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Spending money on events can translate into sales."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stakeholder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person with an interest in a business"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can create publicity by sponsoring events for stakeholders."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "desirability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the quality of being desirable (necessary or useful)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need to boost your product's desirability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mutually"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with mutual action (experienced by two or more people or groups of people) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The relationship is mutually beneficial. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advantageous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "creating favorable conditions that increase the chances of success"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our proposal will be advantageous to your company. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "party"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of people with the same opinions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Polygon and Holly's are the two parties present at the meeting."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le09ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "A core value is a belief that a person or organization views as very important. An example of a core value is \u201cTest everything: assume nothing.\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Work with a partner to research core values of other companies. You can use newspapers or the Internet. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of all the core values you find. Use this list to create a new core value for a PR company."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I understand what a core value is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read and identify different core values."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a new core value. "}]}]}